A: This is a simple case of fuzzy logic, because you have fuzzy relationships among the concepts such as “fasciitis gun”, “recommendation AI”, “powerful massage gun”, etc
One way to write this would be with a language like Python, like
fuzzy = {
    “fasciitis gun”: { “Powerful percussion massage gun”: 0.8, “Theragun Relief”: 0.2 }
}

Then we have something like this for the recommendation algorithm:
fuzzy = {
    “fasciitis”: [
        [ “Powerful percussion massage gun”, 0.8 ], [ “Thera Gun Relieve”, 0.2 ]
    ],
    “recom”: 0.5
}

You can then write something like this for the search:
recommend(fuzzy, ”fasciitis gun”, fuzzy, “recom”)

That will return the second highest weighted string from the list of recommendations. Note that this is not the best answer; for practical purposes, you would probably have to add different weighting parameters for different criteria you might care about.

